{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfmy9nFuVJUM3VzvbMwM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Permanganate cannot be analysed for Dq or B within the ligand-field (Tanabe-Sugano) model, so I am not giving numbers for either.\n\nMn in MnO₄⁻ is Mn(VII), a d⁰ ion. With no d electrons there are no d–d transitions, and the Tanabe-Sugano energy matrices (which describe d-electron term splittings) have no states to fit. The three observed bands are charge-transfer transitions, mainly ligand-to-metal (O 2p → Mn 3d). Their high molar absorptivities (ε ≈ 1 500–2 900 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹, far above the ~1–100 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹ typical of spin- and Laporte-forbidden d–d bands) are consistent with this assignment. Fitting them to Dq and B would give meaningless values, because the model does not describe these excitations.\n\nThe tetrahedral splitting of the oxygen-based orbitals is real, but the energies of these charge-transfer bands depend on metal–ligand orbital overlap and electronegativity, not on the d-orbital Dq and Racah B parameters. A d-d analysis would need a d¹–d⁹ complex with observed d–d bands.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"MnO4- is d0 and its bands are ligand-to-metal charge-transfer transitions, so Dq and B cannot be defined or fitted within the d-d ligand-field model.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8059,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8059,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d020d5e-028e-419c-b0e4-4364aef96d4c","uuid":"6da99d89-ccd9-41ed-aa1c-5aeab982a1d1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T09:42:14.918Z","request_id":"req_011Cgfmy9